                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.24/296: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Burdett</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-12-16T09:00:00-03:00">December 16, 1940—9
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 16—7:45 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>669. For the Under Secretary. Reference Embassy’s telegram 667, December 14, 4
                    p.m. The Minister for Foreign Affairs was informed by the British Ambassador
                    last night that the <hi rendition="#italic">Siqueira Campos</hi> has been
                    released.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Burdett</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
